{{Short description|List of European football squads}}
The following is a list of squads for each national team competing at the [[UEFA Euro 2012|Euro 2012]] in Poland and Ukraine. The tournament started on 8 June 2012 and the [[UEFA Euro 2012 Final|final]] took place in [[Kyiv]] on 1 July 2012.

Each national team had to submit a squad of 23 players by 29 May 2012, three of whom must be goalkeepers.<ref name="French squad">{{cite news | url=http://www.fff.fr/bleus/actu/541744_deux-pre-listes-devoilees-le-9-et-15-mai | language=fr | title=Deux pré-listes dévoilées le 9 et 15 mai |trans-title=Two shortlists unveiled on 9 and 15 May | date=2 May 2012}}</ref> If a player was injured severely enough to prevent his participation in the tournament before his team's first match, he could be replaced by another player.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.uefa.com/multimediafiles/download/competitions/euro/91/87/57/918757_download.pdf |title=Regulations of the UEFA European Football Championship 2006/08 |access-date=2 May 2012 |publisher=UEFA |page=22 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100215034039/http://www.uefa.com/multimediafiles/download/competitions/euro/91/87/57/918757_download.pdf |archive-date=15 February 2010 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

Club memberships are correct as of the 2011–12 season. Caps and goals correct as of 18 June 2012. Ages are correct as of 8 June 2012, the opening day of the tournament.

==Group A==

===Poland===
Manager: [[Franciszek Smuda]]

On 2 May 2012, Smuda named a provisional list of 23 players for the tournament, along with a seven-man reserve list.<ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/history/news/0254-0d7dd2864763-b6a03a6a2380-1000--smuda-picks-poland-s-provisional-euro-squad/ | title=Smuda picks Poland's provisional EURO squad | date=3 May 2012 | work=[[UEFA]] }}</ref> [[Łukasz Fabiański]] withdrew from the squad on 26 May 2012 with a shoulder injury and was replaced by [[Grzegorz Sandomierski]] from the reserve list; Smuda named his 23-man final squad the following day.<ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/history/news/0254-0d7de45ab7c4-53766a115a37-1000--poland-confirm-uefa-euro-2012-party/ | title=Poland confirm UEFA EURO 2012 party | date=27 May 2012 | work=[[UEFA]] }}</ref>

