===Russia===
Manager: {{flagicon|Netherlands}} [[Dick Advocaat]]

On 11 May 2012, Advocaat named a provisional list of 26 players for the tournament.<ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/history/news/0254-0d7dd0f92c47-f27a5bd50cfe-1000--untried-duo-in-provisional-russia-squad/ | work=[[UEFA]] | title=Untried duo in provisional Russia squad | date=11 May 2012}}</ref> [[Vasili Berezutski]] and [[Roman Shishkin]] withdrew on 20 and 24 May respectively, Berezutski with a thigh injury and Shishkin due to a stomach complaint.<ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/history/news/0254-0d7de3b75001-745cf4ae2598-1000--berezutski-ruled-out-of-russia-s-euro-campaign/ | work=[[UEFA]] | title=Berezutski ruled out of Russia's EURO campaign | date=20 May 2012}}</ref><ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/history/news/0254-0d7de3b76d9f-656fe66f15aa-1000--russia-shorn-of-shishkin-for-euro/ | work=[[UEFA]] | title=Russia shorn of Shishkin for EURO | date=24 May 2012}}</ref> Advocaat named his final squad on 25 May 2012; [[Kirill Nababkin]] was named having not been included in the provisional party.<ref>{{cite web | url=http://rfs.ru/main/news/ct131/73916.html| language = ru | title = Advocaat announced the finalized Euro Squad|date=25 May 2012}}</ref>

A 2012 friendly match against Lithuania, recognized by the Russian Football Union but not by FIFA, is not counted for caps.

