==Group C==

===Spain===
Manager: [[Vicente del Bosque]]

Vicente del Bosque named a squad to play in a set of warm-up matches on 15 May 2012, but it did not include any [[FC Barcelona|Barcelona]], [[Athletic Bilbao]] or [[Chelsea F.C.|Chelsea]] players as the two Spanish sides were preparing for the [[2012 Copa del Rey final|Copa del Rey final]] on 25 May, while Chelsea were to take on [[FC Bayern Munich|Bayern Munich]] in the [[2012 UEFA Champions League final|UEFA Champions League final]] on 19 May.<ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/history/news/0254-0d7dd2865a49-15b246a38969-1000--atletico-trio-in-spain-friendly-party/ | title=Atlético trio in Spain friendly party | date=15 May 2012 | publisher=[[UEFA.com]]}}</ref> On 21 May 2012, Del Bosque called-up Chelsea players [[Fernando Torres]] and [[Juan Mata]] for the friendly matches.<ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.fifa.com/worldfootball/news/newsid=1634965.html | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120525103002/http://www.fifa.com/worldfootball/news/newsid=1634965.html | url-status=dead | archive-date=May 25, 2012 | title=Spain add Mata, Torres to squad | date=21 May 2012 | publisher=[[FIFA.com]]}}</ref> On 27 May, Del Bosque gave the final squad list, complete with Barcelona and Athletic Bilbao players.<ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/history/news/0254-0d7de4ff051e-8fe33e17c2b2-1000--holders-spain-include-pedro-in-final-euro-squad/ | title=Holders Spain include Pedro in final EURO squad | date=27 May 2012 | publisher=[[UEFA.com]]}}</ref>

