On 7 May 2012, Giovanni Trapattoni announced his 23-man squad list for Euro 2012, along with a five-man stand-by list.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/history/news/0254-0d7dcfa0ead4-ced9f3e153ec-1000--mccarthy-out-as-trapattoni-names-ireland-squad/|title=McCarthy out as Trapattoni names Ireland squad|date=7 May 2012|publisher=Union of European Football Associations}}</ref> [[Keith Fahey]] withdrew with a groin injury on 26 May and was replaced by [[Paul Green (footballer, born 1983)|Paul Green]].<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/history/news/0254-0d7de7ac2c6b-006e2de0072b-1000--uefa-euro-2012-dream-over-for-ireland-s-fahey/|title=UEFA EURO 2012 dream over for Ireland's Fahey|date=26 May 2012|publisher=Union of European Football Associations}}</ref> On 29 May 2012 [[Kevin Foley (footballer, born 1984)|Kevin Foley]] was replaced by [[Paul McShane (footballer)|Paul McShane]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2012/may/29/euro-2012-republic-ireland-squad|title=Kevin Foley dropped from Republic of Ireland squad|date= 29 May 2012|work=The Guardian|access-date=29 May 2012 }}</ref> The Ireland team was the only squad at the tournament to consist entirely of players from foreign leagues.

