===England===
Manager: [[Roy Hodgson]]

Roy Hodgson announced England's 23-man squad on 16 May 2012, along with a five-man stand-by list.<ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.thefa.com/England/News/2012/euro-2012-squad-announced-160512 |title=Hodgson names Euro 2012 squad|date=16 May 2012 |work=TheFA.com |publisher=The Football Association |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120724080408/https://www.thefa.com/England/News/2012/euro-2012-squad-announced-160512 |archive-date=24 July 2012 |url-status=dead}}</ref> The England team is the only squad to consist entirely of players from their domestic league. On 25 May, [[John Ruddy]] was ruled out with a broken finger; [[Jack Butland]] was called up as his replacement.<ref>{{cite news |title=John Ruddy ruled out of England Euro 2012 squad with injury |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/england/18204979 |work=BBC Sport |publisher=British Broadcasting Corporation |date=25 May 2012 }}</ref> On 28 May, [[Gareth Barry]] was ruled out with a groin injury, being replaced by [[Phil Jagielka]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Euro 2012: Injury rules Gareth Barry out of Euros |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/18232535 |work=BBC Sport |publisher=British Broadcasting Corporation |date=28 May 2012 }}</ref> On 31 May, [[Frank Lampard]] was ruled out with a thigh injury and was replaced by [[Jordan Henderson]].<ref>{{cite news|title=Euro 2012: England's Frank Lampard ruled out through injury|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/18265377|work=BBC Sport|publisher=[[BBC]]|date=31 May 2012}}</ref> On 3 June, [[Gary Cahill]] was ruled out with a double fracture of his jaw and [[Martin Kelly (footballer)|Martin Kelly]] was called up as his replacement.<ref>{{cite news|title=Euro 2012: Gary Cahill ruled out but Rio Ferdinand overlooked|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/0/football/18311737|work=BBC Sport|publisher=[[BBC]]|date=4 June 2012}}</ref>

